---
import PublicPage from '../../components/public/PublicPage.astro';
---

<PublicPage
  label="Legal"
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The rules for using Tosder Communities, publishing templates, and taking part in competitions."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 17, 2026</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Tosder Communities helps travelers discover Cambodia, copy published itineraries into private
      trips, and share reusable templates. We may change or stop features, but we will not silently
      rewrite a finalized competition result.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must be 18 or older and provide accurate account information.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for keeping your password and sessions secure.</li>
      <li>Do not share an account or impersonate another person.</li>
      <li>We may suspend accounts that violate these terms or the community guidelines.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of the text, photos, and itineraries you create. You grant Tosder Communities
      a non-exclusive licence to host, display, copy into traveler trips, and promote that content on
      the service. You confirm you have the rights to every photo and that credits are accurate.
    </p>
    <p>
      Published templates become immutable versions. Travelers who copy a version keep that copy even
      if you later edit or archive the template. You cannot revoke a version from trips that already
      copied it, except through moderation or account deletion processes.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No harassment, hate, threats, spam, or illegal content.</li>
      <li>No unlicensed photos, copied descriptions, or misleading safety advice.</li>
      <li>No attempts to inflate views, likes, saves, qualified uses, or competition rankings.</li>
      <li>No scraping, credential attacks, or interference with the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Competitions and rewards</h2>
    <p>
      Competition rules and prize details are published on the competition page before the period
      starts. Qualified uses are calculated from the server-side ledger. Ties follow the published
      rule. Rewards require a finalized result, administrator approval, and a recorded manual payout.
      No money moves automatically. Voided or corrected results are audited.
    </p>

    <h2>Moderation</h2>
    <p>
      Moderators may hide templates or reviews, warn members, or suspend accounts for violations.
      Decisions are recorded in the audit log and affected members receive an in-app notification.
      Appeals may be escalated to an administrator.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      Travel information can change. Verify opening hours, transport, safety, and prices independently.
      The service is provided as-is to the extent permitted by law. Nothing here is legal, medical, or
      safety advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the service at any time. We may suspend or terminate access for violations,
      fraud, or legal requirements. Provisions about content licences, audit records, and liability
      survive termination.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@tosder.com">hello@tosder.com</a>.</p>

    <p class="note">
      These terms are an operational draft. Legal counsel must review them before public launch.
    </p>
  </article>
</PublicPage>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .updated, .note { color: var(--color-text-subtle); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
  .note { margin-top: var(--space-5); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border); }
  h2 { margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); }
  p, li { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: var(--space-5); }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
